Finding the Lucky Number (Digital Root)

You are given a positive integer N. Your task is to repeatedly sum its digits until only a single digit remains. This final single digit is called the Lucky Number or Digital Root of the number.

Instead of using repeated loops, try to solve this efficiently using the mathematical property of numbers based on divisibility by 9.

Input Format

A single integer N

Constraints

Print a single integer — the digital root of N

Output Format

0 ≤ N ≤ 10^18 N contains only digits Output will always be a single digit (0–9)

Sample Input 0

9875
Sample Output 0

2
Explanation 0

9 + 8 + 7 + 5 = 29 2 + 9 = 11 1 + 1 = 2

Sample Input 1

12345
Sample Output 1

6
Sample Input 2

0
Sample Output 2

0
